  "worked_solution": "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=-i+5j,\\,a=-10j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=3\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(-i+5j)(3)+\\frac{1}{2}(-10j)(3)^{2} \\\\  & =(-3i+15j)+9(-5j) \\\\  & =(-3i+15j)-45j \\\\  & =(-3i-30j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
